IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- P1-art-2.l4 -- ARTICLE 2(1) AND (2): MATERIAL SCOPE.  Layer 1 (P1).
-- Answers one question: is this processing of personal data inside the MATERIAL scope?  Article 2(3)
-- and (4) (Union institutions; Directive 2000/31/EC) and Article 3 (territorial scope) are K2's;
-- whether the Regulation applies in the end needs their answers too (PLAN.md section 4).
-- Whose duty: none; the scope rules create no duty.  Who may rely: a data subject or a controller
-- asking whether the Regulation reaches the processing.
-- ARM ORDER is the encoding's, not the text's (the text states no priority): the exceptions of
-- Art 2(2) are tested before the grant of Art 2(1) (fork F2-1 in NOTES.md).
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 2(1): what the Regulation applies to`

-- src:21 | 1. This Regulation applies to the processing of personal data wholly or partly by automated means and to the processing other than by automated means of personal data which form part of a filing system or are intended to form part of a filing system.
@ref Art 2(1) (src:21)
GIVEN `the operations are processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is wholly or partly by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data form part of a filing system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1) this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the operations are processing of personal data`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Art 2(1) speaks only of "the processing of personal data"
        IF `the processing is wholly or partly by automated means`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- first limb: "the processing of personal data wholly or partly by automated means"
        IF `the personal data form part of a filing system` OR `the personal data are intended to form part of a filing system`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- second limb: "the processing other than by automated means of personal data which form part of a filing system or are intended to form part of a filing system"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to" the two cases named, with no "only"; processing wholly by hand of data that are in no filing system and are not intended to be is neither named nor excluded

§ `Article 2(2): what the Regulation does not apply to`

-- src:22 | 2. This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data:
-- src:23 | (a) in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law;
@ref Art 2(2)(a) (src:22-23)
GIVEN `the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(2)(a) this Regulation applies to processing in the course of an activity outside the scope of Union law` MEANS
    IF `the processing is in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data: (a) in the course of an activity which falls outside the scope of Union law"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (a) excludes only processing in the course of an activity outside Union law; any other processing is not spoken of here

DECLARE `Art 2(2)(d) purpose of the processing` IS ONE OF
    `Art 2(2)(d) prevention of criminal offences`
    `Art 2(2)(d) investigation of criminal offences`
    `Art 2(2)(d) detection of criminal offences`
    `Art 2(2)(d) prosecution of criminal offences`
    `Art 2(2)(d) execution of criminal penalties`
    `Art 2(2)(d) safeguarding against threats to public security`
    `Art 2(2)(d) prevention of threats to public security`
    `Art 2(2)(d) another purpose`

-- src:22 | 2. This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data:
-- src:24 | (b) by the Member States when carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU;
@ref Art 2(2)(b) (src:22-24)
GIVEN `the processing is by a Member State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(2)(b) this Regulation applies to processing by the Member States in activities within Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU` MEANS
    IF `the processing is by a Member State` AND `the Member State is carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data: ... (b) by the Member States when carrying out activities which fall within the scope of Chapter 2 of Title V of the TEU"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (b) excludes only the Member States, and only when carrying out those activities

-- src:22 | 2. This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data:
-- src:25 | (c) by a natural person in the course of a purely personal or household activity;
@ref Art 2(2)(c) (src:22-25)
GIVEN `the processing is by a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(2)(c) this Regulation applies to processing by a natural person in the course of a purely personal or household activity` MEANS
    IF `the processing is by a natural person` AND `the natural person processes in the course of a purely personal or household activity`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data: ... (c) by a natural person in the course of a purely personal or household activity"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (c) excludes only a natural person, and only in a purely personal or household activity; a company, or a person acting for business, is not spoken of here

-- src:22 | 2. This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data:
-- src:26 | (d) by competent authorities for the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security.
@ref Art 2(2)(d) (src:22-26)
GIVEN `the processing is by a competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose of the processing` IS AN `Art 2(2)(d) purpose of the processing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(2)(d) this Regulation applies to processing by competent authorities for the purposes of criminal justice and public security` MEANS
    IF `the processing is by a competent authority`
       AND NOT (`the purpose of the processing` EQUALS `Art 2(2)(d) another purpose`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data: ... (d) by competent authorities for the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): point (d) excludes only competent authorities, and only for those purposes
    -- "competent authorities" is a term the text does not define here (see recital 19, which names Directive (EU) 2016/680; that instrument is not among the sources); `the processing is by a competent authority` is taken as a plain input fact.

@ref Art 2(2), the chapeau with points (a) to (d) (src:22-26)
GIVEN `result of point (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `result of point (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `result of point (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `result of point (d)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(2) this Regulation applies to the processing of personal data, given points (a) to (d)` MEANS
    IF `result of point (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR `result of point (b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR `result of point (c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
       OR `result of point (d)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data"
    ELSE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 2(2) says what the Regulation does not apply to; for any other processing it is silent

§ `Article 2(1) and (2) together: the material scope`

@ref Art 2(1) and (2): the exceptions are tested first (the order is the encoding's)
GIVEN `the answer of Art 2(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of Art 2(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 2(1) and (2) the processing is within the material scope of this Regulation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of Art 2(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Regulation does not apply to the processing of personal data"
        IF `the answer of Art 2(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither Art 2(1) nor Art 2(2) speaks of this processing
